**CONFIRMED-WITH-GAPS** — T227’s packet and register agree on the core mechanic, the 9–14 s technique window, and the named evidence. The reveal timing and archived-media checks remain open for Cycle 039 Wave 36 §1 Observe.

1. **Flesh onset needs firsthand confirmation.** Both catalogue entries describe green flesh as the blade completes its pass. The supplied Observe record §1.2 and §1.3 CP2–CP4 instead reports flesh absent at source 11 s, visible at 12 s while the blade is still cutting, and established by 13 s. The catalogue wording supports the state at completion but leaves onset unspecified. The reported frames bracket onset to **(11, 12] s**. The evidence JPEG and census frames were unavailable for independent inspection. The underlying edit type remains unresolved in both catalogue entries. [Packet #13 digest §T04](/home/hatch/workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study/video-digests/2026-11-17-yt-dnjdjiwcfy/digest.md:36) · [Style-library §T227](/home/hatch/workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study/style-library/techniques-transitions.md:306)
2. **Technique window and reference clip have different bounds.** The digest and register agree on **9–14 s**, which gives **5.000 s** by subtraction. The digest separately lists the reference clip at **9–16 s**, a nominal **7.000 s** that overlaps the start of T05 at 14 s. The archived probe record lists a total duration of 100.894 s, which places the technique window within the recorded runtime. The archived `source.mp4` and reference clip were unavailable, so the endpoint frames and reported measured clip duration are **NOT ASSESSED**. [Digest §§T04–T05](/home/hatch/workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study/video-digests/2026-11-17-yt-dnjdjiwcfy/digest.md:36) · [Style-library §T227](/home/hatch/workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study/style-library/techniques-transitions.md:306) · [Archived probe record](/home/hatch/workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study/video-digests/2026-11-17-yt-dnjdjiwcfy/probe.json:2)
3. **Prior-attempt findings are limited to the staged record.** The staged recreation verdict history has zero matches for the three named IDs, T227, T232, and T234. The register lists T227 as owed #102, T232 as owed #103 with its own dicing mechanic, and T234 as an episode that reuses T227’s mechanism without a separate obligation. The supplied §1.5 describes T234 as sharing the wave’s first-attempt status, while the register establishes only its mechanism and obligation. A separate T234 attempt is unverified. No score claim surfaced for arithmetic or return binding. **Lens count assessed: 0.** [Recreation verdict history](/home/hatch/workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study-jobs/recreation/verdict-history.md) · [Technique register](/home/hatch/workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study/style-library/TECHNIQUES.md:151) · [Style-library §T234](/home/hatch/workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study/style-library/techniques-transitions.md:331)
4. **Packet adoption gaps do not attach to T04.** Cycle-020 records that G1 concerned uncited PES cards and G2 concerned the T06 bowl state. Both were cured before the packet was adopted clean. [Digestion verdict history](/home/hatch/workspace/jobs/sync-staging/study-jobs/video-digestion/verdict-history.md:72)

